            <ArticleTitle>National athletic trainers' association position statement: preventing sudden death in sports.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>96-118</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present recommendations for the prevention and screening, recognition, and treatment of the most common conditions resulting in sudden death in organized sports.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Cardiac conditions, head injuries, neck injuries, exertional heat stroke, exertional sickling, asthma, and other factors (eg, lightning, diabetes) are the most common causes of death in athletes.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RECOMMENDATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">These guidelines are intended to provide relevant information on preventing sudden death in sports and to give specific recommendations for certified athletic trainers and others participating in athletic health care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
